 "mechanism_choice": "Forest SUPPRESSES grass fire (Staver-Levin mesic): flammability sig(B-theta) is carried by grass fine fuel only; mature canopy shades grass (space term 1-B-cT*T keeps B below theta under canopy) so fire cannot enter forest. Canopy megafires excluded deliberately: (a) they belong to a different (crown-fire) regime, (b) they would add a second fast clock that destroys L3 simplicity. Negative control veg_flam=0.8 shows flammable canopy kills bistability (forest burns like grass -> savanna everywhere).",
 "theory_coords": [
  "R=gT/g succession slowness",
  "W=mu/gT senescence balance",
  "Tm fire-trap maturity threshold",
  "kapT trap severity",
  "cT canopy shading of grass",
  "rhoT tree seed rain",
  "patch_frac/Tinit_patch mosaic geometry",
  "gT = tree growth price (G3)"
 ],
